# Text files check out with LF on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS HERE MORE THAN USUALLY. The dashboard's JavaScript, CSS and
# HTML are EMBEDDED IN THE BINARY with go:embed, and their bytes are what the
# ETag is computed from (see staticAssets in internal/webui/server.go). A Windows
# checkout without this converts them to CRLF, so the same source produces a
# different binary and a different validator — and a test that looks for "\n}\n"
# in app.js to prove the verdict still derives its colours from the shared
# mapping simply stops finding it. That test failed on the first Windows CI run
# for exactly this reason, having nothing to do with what it was guarding.
#
# The documentation is embedded too, and the exported manual is written from it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
